  "reviewed_boundaries": [
    "Only public task cases, the disclosed representation and actual public RPC feedback enter model history. Hidden evaluation is terminal and never appended to model history.",
    "Failed request raw streams and recoverable usage are retained. Unknown usage or an incomplete denominator disables the descriptive advantage gate.",
    "Per-cell wall time includes inference, tool checks, native compilation, terminal hidden execution and owned-process cleanup. Shared setup and controls remain separate; human review time is unknown, not zero.",
    "Reviewer is separate from the study-runner author, but contributed the audited Rust fixture and its tests after discovering the acceptance bypass; this is an internal independent review, not an external third-party audit."
  ],
  "reviewer": "/root/core_contracts",
  "schema": "hepta.hia.agent-public-tools.independent-review.v1",
  "scope_limits": [
    "Only this frozen four-task/eight-cell descriptive pilot is authorized by this methodological review; no result or language advantage is presumed.",
    "Rust candidates use the disclosed restricted lexical/API profile. Token bans also affect comments and strings; the pilot does not represent arbitrary safe Rust development.",
    "Audited Vec evidence observes the selected safe API, not every process allocation or machine store instruction. IndexMut observes mutable access and subsequent actual readback; zero-to-zero assignment is not distinguished from taking a mutable reference.",
    "HIA operation evidence is actual VM execution, not machine-code refinement. No cross-language semantic equivalence proof is claimed.",
    "Task-information isolation is not an OS-hermeticity claim against malicious generated code. Provider cache and scheduling are not controlled; population-level productivity and human-cost advantage are not established."
